  reel_script says the union demanded that 41 months be regularised as service period, and the article says the 41-month dismissal period should be regularised as service period per the High Court ruling; the draft's wording 'பணி காலமாக' is fine, but the reel_script omits that the dismissal was in 2002 for road-department road workers and the 41 months are the dismissal period (draft says 'பணி நீக்கம் செய்யப்பட்ட நெடுஞ்சாலைத் துறை பணியாளர்கள் 41 மாதம் பணி காலமாக' which reads as if the workers themselves are 41 months of service, a meaning shift)
  reel_script says the computer assistants should be appointed on time-scale pay but omits that they work through outside agency in revenue, agriculture and horticulture departments
  reel_script omits the important fact that the demand for the sanctioned vacancies to be filled immediately was not clearly stated in the text as the demand ordering; minor but the slides_spec 'மற்ற கோரிக்கைகள்' line 'வாரிசு நியமனம் 5 சதவீதத்தில் இருந்து 25 சதவீதமாக உயர்த்த' is ungrammatically truncated and lacks a clear meaning in Tamil
  reel_script omits that the union also demanded the government take over fixing the new medical insurance scheme's irregularities, and draft says 'அரசே ஏற்க வேண்டும்' attaching it to the irregularities, which mixes two facts into one sentence
  reel_script says the Avinashi Taluk office meeting was 'சந்திப்பு' while the article says it was a 'பிரசார இயக்கம' (campaign movement) organised by Tamil Nadu Government Employees Union; the draft omits that it was a campaign and the state union organisation detail
